    "40": {
      "issue": 40,
      "title": "Paginate the export endpoint",
      "body": "Exports return every row at once. Page them with an opaque cursor.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `GET /export?cursor=\u2026` returns at most 500 rows and a `next` cursor.\n- Rows inserted during a paged read are not skipped.",
      "state": "closed",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:3030/bottown/demo/issues/40"
    },
    "42": {
      "issue": 42,
      "title": "Retry webhook deliveries with backoff",
      "body": "Webhook deliveries are tried **once**; a 5xx or a timeout drops the event.\n\nRetry with exponential backoff and jitter, up to 6 attempts over ~1 hour.\n\n```go\ntype Retry struct { Attempts int; Base time.Duration }\n```",
      "state": "open",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:3030/bottown/demo/issues/42"
    },
    "44": {
      "issue": 44,
      "title": "Should exports stream CSV or build it in memory?",
      "body": "Exports can reach 2 GB. Should the endpoint stream CSV rows as they are read, or build the file and serve it?\n\nThis is a question for a discuss run, not an implementation.",
      "state": "open",
      "url": "http://127.0.0.1:3030/bottown/demo/issues/44"
    },
    "47": {
